{#-
    INTERFACE (stable, shared by every leaderboard - docs/features/xp-levels/ux-polish/design-spec.md §8.4, WCAG 2.4.3 + 4.1.3):
    After the gap row or "Show more" revealed rows: focus moves to the first new row, and a polite live region says what
    came. Render it (anywhere in the re-rendered part) only in the response to such a tap:
      {{ include('leaderboards/_window_announcer.html.twig', {
          focus_id: 'board-row-…',                    the id of the first new row (a <tr id>)
          reveal: {from: 26, to: 75}, total: 7878,     what was revealed (LeaderboardWindow::gapReveal() / showMoreReveal() of
                                                       the window BEFORE the tap), 1-based positions
      }) }}
    In a Live Component: keep the reveal of the last action in a prop and render this with it - the values change, so
    leaderboard_window_controller.js runs again after the morph.
-#}
<div
    hidden
    data-controller="leaderboard-window"
    data-leaderboard-window-focus-value="{{ focus_id }}"
    data-leaderboard-window-announce-value="{{ 'leaderboards.announce'|trans({'%from%': reveal.from|format_number, '%to%': reveal.to|format_number, '%total%': total|format_number}) }}"
></div>
